{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Please do not leave us.</b> Let your children go as officers with us." "<b>For therefore you know our encampments in the wilderness.</b> And if your children too abandon us, you will profane HaShem in the eyes of the nations, for they will say: if Jethro had truly seen in them a divine matter, he and his sons would not have left them. On this Moses, Jethro, and his sons agreed — for indeed Jethro returned to his land, as it says (Exodus 18:27), וַיְשַׁלַּח מֹשֶׁה אֶת חֹתְנוֹ וַיֵּלֶךְ לוֹ אֶל אַרְצוֹ, and his children went with Israel without doubt, as he testified in the book of Judges, saying (Judges 1:16), וּבְנֵי קֵינִי חֹתֵן מֹשֶׁה עָלוּ מֵעִיר הַתְּמָרִים אֶת בְּנֵי יְהוּדָה."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:15.916506404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}